hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24295","Yazid narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, Hasan narrated to us, Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to us: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to some people and withheld from some people. So it reached him that they blamed him, so he addressed the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: I gave to some people and left some people, and they blamed me. And I give the gift to a man while another is more beloved to me than him, and I only give them because of what is in their hearts of panic and distress, and I withhold from a people because of what Allah has placed in their hearts of richness and good, among them Amr ibn Taghlib. Amr said: The word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not please me in exchange for red camels."
"24296","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, I heard Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Amr ibn Taghlib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour are that wealth overflows and increases, the pen appears, and trade spreads. He said: Amr said: A man would sell a sale and say: Until I consult the merchant of Banu so-and-so, and one seeks in the great quarter for a scribe and none is found."
